class_name Maps
extends RefCounted

## Every map is a grid of characters, one per tile (TILE metres square). Edit the rows to change a
## layout: all rows of a map must be the same length, and a map needs exactly one P.
## The camera looks from the bottom-right corner of the grid, so on screen the grid appears turned
## 45 degrees clockwise: the top-left of the text is the top of the screen.
##
##   #  wall                        w  wall with a window (ship) or a glowing vent (missions)
##   .  floor                       ,  floor detail (grating on metal maps, ash on the ash map)
##   =  hazard stripes / cracks     ~  pit: void, molten slag or lava. Blocks walking; shots fly over
##   o  pillar / rock spire         t  console or machine (solid)
##   c  crate (breaks for scrap in missions, solid cargo on the ship)
##   $  scrap cache                 +  repair kit
##   P  player start                X  extraction pad (powers up when the boss falls)
##   s  scuttler   g  gunner   b  bruiser   B  the map's boss
##   Q  quartermaster   A  augment bay   L  weapons lab   M  mission table   (ship only)

